    "markdown": "---\ntitle: Diagnosing dengue fever\nauthor: Alex Reinhart\ndate: October 21, 2026\ndescription: Dengue fever is a common illness in tropical and subtropical parts of the world. Definitive diagnosis requires dengue-specific lab tests, but it may be possible to get an accurate diagnosis from cheaper and easier tests and symptoms. Use data on dengue patients in Vietnam to evaluate whether a classifier can accurately diagnose dengue from blood tests and symptoms.\ncategories:\n  - classification\n  - logistic regression\ndata:\n  year: 2015\n  files: dengue.csv\n---\n\n## Motivation\n\nDengue fever is a common viral illness spread by mosquitoes in tropical and\nsubtropical parts of the world. More than 5 million people are infected each\nyear. While most people recover within one or two weeks, some cases become\nsevere, requiring hospitalization to treat shock and internal bleeding. Roughly\n5,000 people die of dengue fever each year.\n\nWhile there is no medication that can cure dengue, prompt diagnosis is still\nhelpful so patients can get supportive treatment and be closely monitored for\nsigns of severe dengue. This data comes from a study in Vietnam which tested\nwhether simple lab tests and symptom data can be used to accurately diagnose\ndengue fever, rather than relying on more expensive dengue-specific lab tests.\nIf this were possible, doctors could diagnose patients more quickly and cheaply,\nbefore more extensive lab test results are available.\n\n## Data\n\nThe data contains symptom and test results for 5,726 patients, all children\n1--15 years old in several hospitals in Vietnam. Children were eligible to\nenroll if they had been sick less than 72 hours and had a fever, and the\nattending physician thought dengue fever was a possible diagnosis. Patients\nwhose parents consented were enrolled in the study. On enrollment, blood samples\nwere drawn for normal blood tests (such as white blood counts) and dengue fever\ntests.\n\nIf the patient was hospitalized, a second blood sample was drawn for additional\nblood tests to see if they had dengue fever antibodies. Of those patients who\nwere *not* hospitalized, 10% were randomly selected to get a second blood\nsample.\n\nThe definitive diagnosis of dengue fever was made by using three tests: RT-PCR,\nserology, and ELISA assay.\n\n### Data preview\n\n<h4><a href=\" https://cmustatistics.github.io/data-repository/data/dengue.csv \"> dengue.csv </a></h4>\n<div data-pagedtable=\"false\">\n  <script data-pagedtable-source type=\"application/json\">\n{\"columns\":[{\"label\":[\"DateEnrol\"],\"name\":[1],\"type\":[\"chr\"],\"align\":[\"left\"]},{\"label\":[\"SiteNo\"],\"name\":[2],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"StudyNo\"],\"name\":[3],\"type\":[\"chr\"],\"align\":[\"left\"]},{\"label\":[\"Sex\"],\"name\":[4],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Age\"],\"name\":[5],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"DayDisease\"],\"name\":[6],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Vomiting\"],\"name\":[7],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Abdo\"],\"name\":[8],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Muco\"],\"name\":[9],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Skin\"],\"name\":[10],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Temp\"],\"name\":[11],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"BMI\"],\"name\":[12],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Height\"],\"name\":[13],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Weight\"],\"name\":[14],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Flush\"],\"name\":[15],\"type\":[\"lgl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Hepatomegaly\"],\"name\":[16],\"type\":[\"lgl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Rash\"],\"name\":[17],\"type\":[\"lgl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Injection\"],\"name\":[18],\"type\":[\"lgl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"WBC\"],\"name\":[19],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"HCT\"],\"name\":[20],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"PLT\"],\"name\":[21],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"NEUCount\"],\"name\":[22],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"LYMCount\"],\"name\":[23],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"MONOCount\"],\"name\":[24],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"ALB\"],\"name\":[25],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"AST\"],\"name\":[26],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"ALT\"],\"name\":[27],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"CK\"],\"name\":[28],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Lab_Confirmed_Dengue\"],\"name\":[29],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Serotype\"],\"name\":[30],\"type\":[\"chr\"],\"align\":[\"left\"]},{\"label\":[\"NS1_PLATELIA\"],\"name\":[31],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"NS1_TRIP\"],\"name\":[32],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"SeroConversion\"],\"name\":[33],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"Serology\"],\"name\":[34],\"type\":[\"chr\"],\"align\":[\"left\"]},{\"label\":[\"Pairedsample\"],\"name\":[35],\"type\":[\"chr\"],\"align\":[\"left\"]}],\"data\":[{\"1\":\"10/19/10 12:00 AM\",\"2\":\"1\",\"3\":\"1-0001\",\"4\":\"1\",\"5\":\"11\",\"6\":\"3\",\"7\":\"1\",\"8\":\"1\",\"9\":\"2\",\"10\":\"2\",\"11\":\"36.8\",\"12\":\"16.39660\",\"13\":\"144\",\"14\":\"34.0\",\"15\":\"FALSE\",\"16\":\"FALSE\",\"17\":\"FALSE\",\"18\":\"FALSE\",\"19\":\"5.37\",\"20\":\"37.8\",\"21\":\"110\",\"22\":\"3.52\",\"23\":\"1.51\",\"24\":\"0.31\",\"25\":\"41.7\",\"26\":\"147\",\"27\":\"69\",\"28\":\"155\",\"29\":\"1\",\"30\":\"2\",\"31\":\"1\",\"32\":\"1\",\"33\":\"1\",\"34\":\"2\",\"35\":\"1\"},{\"1\":\"10/19/10 12:00 AM\",\"2\":\"1\",\"3\":\"1-0002\",\"4\":\"1\",\"5\":\